    "from": "tour2020",
    "text": "Photos above:\n\nSights along the way from Tucson, through the Tohono O'odham Native Land Reserve,  on to Why, Ajo, and Gila Bend.  Amazing southwest USA desert scenery. Water is scarce, with long, isolated roads.\n\nAll along the way since New Mexico, there have been signs of organized illegal immigration, where I have found a passport, cellphone, military grade backpacks,  outdoor wear, food and hydration supplies, and other discarded essentials.  There have been many such survival caches abandoned along the side of the road invisible to the automotive traffic.",
